We consider two popular evaluation metrics: coverage and accuracy. Given a compute allocation
c(xi), coverage evaluates whether any of the c(xi) generations in g(xi; c(xi)) correctly answers the
query xi, while accuracy evaluates whether the final output f(xi; c(xi)) is correct. These metrics are
defined as:
Coverage(xi; c(xi)) := I{there exists y ∈g(xi; c(xi)) that correctly answers query xi.}
Accuracy(xi; c(xi)) := I{f(xi; c(xi)) correctly answers query xi.}

